    "created_at": "2016-02-01T16:09:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-01T16:09:19Z",
    "body": "The promise-vending `play()` is now [live in the spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-media-play), so for everyone who did not follow along in the pull request, here's a summary.\n\nEvery call to `play()` returns a promise, which will be resolved at the same time that the `playing` event is fired. If we were already playing, the promise will be resolved with the same timing, but without first firing a `playing` event.\n\nThere are two ways for `play()` to return an already-rejected promise, and that is \"if the user agent or the system does not allow media playback in the current context\" (mobile autoplay blocking) and if the resource selection algorithm has already failed with `MEDIA_ERR_SRC_NOT_SUPPORTED`, as playback cannot succeed without loading another resource.\n\nThe promise rejections that happen outside the `play()` method are more complicated. There are ways for the promise to be left unsettled when it seems like we should be able to reject it, specifically in the case of network and decode errors. In https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/509#issuecomment-174967812 and https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/509#issuecomment-177914176 I say some uncharitable things about how error handling currently works. If left unsettled, promises will be rejected on the next pause of invocation of the media element load algorithm.\n\nKnown issues that would improve upon the current spec:\n- [Wait for media playback to really start before firing the playing event](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/309)\n- [Revisit how fatal and non-fatal media network/decode/abort errors work](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/346)\n\nFinally, for everyone who likes promises, there are also issues for promisifying [`pause()`](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/310), [`load()`](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/554) and a new [`seek()`](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/553).\n",
